  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2fe6c405-c8b6-55de-8471-989230bf36c5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=3 \\\\ x &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **III.** The system is inconsistent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0d7a0ee9-b885-5ad7-9cf1-2952b967123c",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
